# PHP Laravel Standards (caveman)

- Use PHP 8.5+ features when useful.
- Always `declare(strict_types=1);` in php files.
- Always braces in control flow.
- Use explicit param + return types.
- Use constructor property promotion.
- Use `#[Override]` when overriding.
- Use static method/closure when no external state.

- Naming:
  - Class: PascalCase.
  - Method/property: camelCase.
  - Local var + private prop: snake_case.
  - DB column: snake_case.
  - Constant: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE.
  - Enum case: PascalCase.

- Keep code simple, modular, reusable.
- Prefer interfaces/traits/abstractions for shared logic.
- PHPDoc in English. Inline comments.
- For suppressions: be specific, explain why, prefer better typing over ignore.

- Laravel details live in `laravel-boost.mdc`.
